Why ping works but curl doesn’t — same server, same VPC.

Have you ever been in a situation where:

ping server-A
works fine, but

curl http://server-A:8080
just hangs forever? 😅

This is one of those classic “networking in DevOps” moments that separates “it’s reachable” from “it’s serving.”

 Here’s what’s happening:
Ping works at ICMP (Layer 3) — it just checks reachability.
Curl works at TCP (Layer 4) — it depends on open ports, security groups, and app availability.

So yes, your network is fine… but your service isn’t.
